    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2014-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The sum inside the parentheses is \\(\\dfrac12+\\dfrac15+\\dfrac{1}{10}=\\dfrac{5+2+1}{10}=\\dfrac{4}{5}.\\)\n\nIts reciprocal is \\(\\dfrac54,\\) so the expression equals \\(10\\cdot\\dfrac54=\\dfrac{25}{2}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Add the three fractions inside the parentheses first",
        "\\(\\dfrac12+\\dfrac15+\\dfrac{1}{10}=\\dfrac{8}{10}\\), then take the reciprocal and multiply by \\(10\\)"
      ],
